  "body": "Both the in-dashboard Guide and `docs/USAGE.md` still told the reader to *\"paste a key, press **Validate**, then **Apply** and select it as active\"*. After 4.39.0–4.40.1 none of that is the flow — and one clause was **never** true: there is no \"active provider\" to select, the model ref on Model Config decides who serves a request.\n\nA walkthrough that names a button which does not exist is worse than no walkthrough, because its reader cannot tell \"I misread this\" from \"this lies\".\n\n## What they say now\n\nSearch for the provider — the box matches name, id **and** variable name, so `GROQ_API_KEY` finds Groq. Press **Configure** to open its key pool. Paste into **Add key**, several comma-separated if you like. **Keys save immediately and do not need Apply.** Rotation *does* need Apply, and restarts the server. **Refresh models** is the real API call, so a model count is the confirmation that a key works. Local backends offer **Test connection** instead.\n\nThe \"reading validation failures\" table is now \"reading a failed **Refresh models**\" — the control that actually produces those status codes.\n\n**README:** two stale routes fixed. `Providers → Manage keys` is no longer the path, and the per-provider button is Refresh models, not Test.\n\n## The guard, not just the fix\n\nPart IX has carried *\"docs drift is unguarded\"* as a known gap for a long time, and it finally cost something. `tests/contracts/test_docs_ui_labels.py` now pins every control name the docs instruct the reader to press, and fails if the dashboard stops defining it.\n\n**That guard took three attempts to be worth having, and both faults were found only by breaking it deliberately:**\n\n1. It searched `index.html` wholesale — but **the Guide lives in `index.html`**, so it matched the Guide's own prose and passed regardless of whether the control existed. The Guide view is now cut out of the surface it searches.\n2. It substring-matched, so after renaming *both* real \"Refresh models\" buttons it still found the hint string `\"No discovered models. Refresh models or enter a custom slug.\"` and passed. It now requires the label as a fully quoted JS string, or as element text in the markup.\n\nVerified failing **by name** two different ways, and passing on restore:\n\n```\nbreak: rename the two real buttons in admin.js\n  FAILED test_documented_control_exists_in_the_dashboard[Refresh models]\n\nbreak: rename a static button in index.html\n  FAILED test_documented_control_exists_in_the_dashboard[Validate]\n\nrestored\n  13 passed\n```\n\n```\nruff format / ruff check / ty: clean\npytest: 3328 passed, 6 failed\n```\n\nThe 6 are the documented PowerShell installer baseline, identical on unmodified `main` in the same shell.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **The screenshot in USAGE.md's provider section is stale** — it is `assets/admin-requests.png`, which is both mis-named for its caption (\"Provider configuration in the Admin UI\") and predates several redesigns. Refreshing it needs a browser and a server with real traffic; neither is reachable in this session. Left as flagged debt rather than silently shipped as current.\n- The guard checks control *names*, not prose accuracy. Nothing can check prose — but names are what goes stale first and silently.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
