    "message": "docs: the Guide and USAGE described a Providers page that no longer exists\n\nBoth the in-dashboard Guide and docs/USAGE.md still told the reader to \"paste a\nkey, press Validate, then Apply and select it as active\". After 4.39.0-4.40.1\nnone of that is the flow, and one clause was never true at all: there is no\n\"active provider\" to select -- the model ref on Model Config decides who serves\na request. A walkthrough that names a button which does not exist is worse than\nno walkthrough, because its reader cannot tell \"I misread this\" from \"this\nlies\".\n\nWhat they say now: search for the provider (the box matches name, id and\nvariable name, so GROQ_API_KEY finds Groq), press Configure to open its key\npool, paste into Add key -- several comma-separated if you like -- and note that\nkeys save immediately and do not need Apply. Rotation does need Apply and\nrestarts the server. Refresh models is the real API call, so a model count is\nthe confirmation that a key works. Local backends offer Test connection\ninstead. The \"reading validation failures\" table is now \"reading a failed\nRefresh models\", which is the control that produces those codes.\n\nREADME: two stale routes fixed. \"Providers -> Manage keys\" is no longer the\npath, and the per-provider button is Refresh models, not Test.\n\nPart IX has carried \"docs drift is unguarded\" as a known gap for a long time\nand it finally cost something, so this adds the guard rather than only the fix.\ntests/contracts/test_docs_ui_labels.py pins every control name the docs\ninstruct the reader to press, and fails if the dashboard stops defining it.\n\nThat guard took three attempts to be worth having, and both faults were found\nonly by breaking it deliberately:\n\n  1. It searched index.html wholesale -- but the Guide LIVES in index.html, so\n     it matched the Guide's own prose and passed regardless. The Guide view is\n     now cut out of the surface it searches.\n  2. It substring-matched, so after renaming both real \"Refresh models\"\n     buttons it still found the hint string \"No discovered models. Refresh\n     models or enter a custom slug.\" and passed. It now requires the label as a\n     fully quoted JS string or as element text in the markup.\n\nVerified failing by name for a JS rename (Refresh models) and an HTML rename\n(Validate), and passing on restore.\n\n  ruff format / ruff check / ty: clean\n  pytest: 3328 passed, 6 failed -- the documented PowerShell installer\n  baseline, identical on unmodified main in the same shell\n\nNot done: the screenshot in USAGE.md's provider section is still\nassets/admin-requests.png, which is both mis-named for its caption and predates\nseveral redesigns. Refreshing it needs a browser and a server with traffic;\nneither is reachable here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
